00:00:58.260 --> 00:00:59.980
This video was shot on fuji400

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:05.440
Some profiles have been modified, and the
first one is vektro100

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:09.159
the only modification brought to this profile
is the decrease in the black point which was

00:01:09.159 --> 00:01:13.140
lowered to -15 for even more contrast

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:17.461
Next on the list is the fuji400
I changed the Black level +3

00:01:17.461 --> 00:01:23.440
Knee to 80% +1
and the biggest modification is the reduction

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:28.600
of the saturation to +5 which is not even
a modification itself, because the original

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:32.880
profile had +5 from the begining but i might
have had a typo when making the graphics for

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:37.049
the video, so sorry for that

00:01:37.049 --> 00:01:43.580
next profile is portra 800
the initial portra800 was made for a candy

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:51.159
look but nowadays i'm using portra800 for
a variety of projects so i need a more natural

00:01:51.159 --> 00:01:53.320
look.

00:01:53.320 --> 00:02:03.070
First thing black gamma narrow +7
i brought down the saturation down

00:02:03.070 --> 00:02:09.299
color phase to 0 or -2 depending on preferences
and in the color depth it's going to be

00:02:09.299 --> 00:02:13.280
Red +3
Green +5

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:18.160
Blue +4
Cyan -4

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:21.670
Magenta -3
Yellow -3

00:02:21.670 --> 00:02:28.220
Next profile that i've changed i kodak gold
Set the black level from -15 to -10 because

00:02:28.220 --> 00:02:34.880
i felt it was maybe too contrasty
Black gamma wide -7

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:43.200
change the color mode from s-gamut3 to s-gamut
simple because i noticed how s-gamut3 was

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:55.550
shifting parts of the yellow spectrum towards
magenta and 

00:02:55.550 --> 00:03:05.489
s-gamut is overall more even with the yellows
which is exactly what i want.

00:03:05.489 --> 00:03:09.220
These are the modifications that have been
made to the profiles.

00:03:09.220 --> 00:03:13.800
Now let's see how to shoot the film profiles?

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:20.819
Initially, i made the film profiles for myself,
but they came out so good i had to share them

00:03:20.819 --> 00:03:22.700
with the everybody else.

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:30.960
with that in mind, my style is darker, moody
with athypical color schemes, and some people

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:38.930
might say stuff like '' ohh your shots are
underexposed and the skin color isn't accurate"

00:03:38.930 --> 00:03:45.640
this is my personal style, in commercial work
i shoot differently

00:03:45.640 --> 00:03:50.420
but right now we are shooting artistically

00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:57.959
so for a general guide, besides portra 800
which i overexpose by 1 or 2 stops,with the

00:03:57.959 --> 00:04:08.580
rest of the profiles I usually underexpose
by one stop or even 2-3 stops and in the color

00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:11.060
filter i go for a green cyanish look

00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:17.129
not all profiles go with that so i will give
you general guides you can start with when

00:04:17.129 --> 00:04:18.239
shooting each profile

00:04:18.239 --> 00:04:23.560
Pp1 Vektor100
usually i like a green cyan look so i use

00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:31.320
c3g1.5 nighttime i usually shoot 3900 or 4200
with a yellow filter giving it a super warm

00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:32.320
look.

00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:34.949
Pp2 Senova Light
usually lower kelvin and enhanced reds or

00:04:34.949 --> 00:04:37.460
magentas so i shift it towards a3 or m3

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:39.970
Pp3Fuji400
this actually works well in both colder and

00:04:39.970 --> 00:04:45.470
warmer tones, so go for cyan green look or
sometimes just lift up the kelvin by 500-1000

00:04:45.470 --> 00:04:48.530
Pp4 classic chrome
this profile is still under development but

00:04:48.530 --> 00:04:52.740
from what i've been experimenting is work
really well with warmer tones, so at the moment

00:04:52.740 --> 00:04:58.190
i would shoot correct temperature or above
and bring the color filter towards red magenta

00:04:58.190 --> 00:05:02.229
pp5 Evpro+
is a versatile profile, but usually i shoot

00:05:02.229 --> 00:05:06.031
colder with this profile, so maybe try going
2000k bellow normal and add a green tint to

00:05:06.031 --> 00:05:07.031
it

00:05:07.031 --> 00:05:09.350
Pp6 Ektar100 usually colder tones, or hot
magentas, so shift the color filter towards

00:05:09.350 --> 00:05:10.650
either cyan or red

00:05:10.650 --> 00:05:14.220
Pp7 Portra 800again, a very versatile profile
with super soft gradations

00:05:14.220 --> 00:05:15.990
will look good anyway you push it.

00:05:15.990 --> 00:05:23.780
if you want to get a more warmer tone just
like in the movie 'Her' , shoot 500-1000 kelvin

00:05:23.780 --> 00:05:26.280
above normal shift the filter towards magenta
to get a soft dreamy look

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:30.350
Pp8 Kodak gold
definitelly go hot, 1000 k-2000k higher than

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:33.410
normal and shift the color filter towards
magenta red

00:05:33.410 --> 00:05:37.699
pp09 Eterna Simulation, High Fidelity
haven't tested too much with this profile

00:05:37.699 --> 00:05:48.820
but you can try any of the above and let us
know in the comments if you find any interesting

00:05:48.820 --> 00:05:49.820
settings

00:05:49.820 --> 00:05:55.180
Pp10 i'm going nostalgic with this one, so
take it to magenta blue to accentuate the

00:05:55.180 --> 00:05:56.180
natural earthy tones

00:05:56.180 --> 00:06:00.680
You can also go into the extremes if you want
a more artistic look, definitely nothing wrong

00:06:00.680 --> 00:06:06.870
with that, just try to feel the mood and what
colors the scene is asking for.

00:06:06.870 --> 00:06:15.200
Guys, these are only suggestions, not golden
rules, and even rules are made to be broken,

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:19.970
otherwise nothing great would be created.

00:06:19.970 --> 00:06:26.590
So try them out and experiment, because that
what this is about

